#lesson(58, drills: (70, 71, 72))[
  == Caution to the Student

  Never begin to practice until you are sure you know how. Languid, thoughtless
  practice should be avoided. Put ambition, put energy, put the fire of
  determined will behind your practice, and the results will be astonishing.
  Take advantage of all favorable conditions. Not only keep the muscles of the
  right arm in a relaxed condition, but guard against tension in any part of the
  body. Keep the side of the hand and the wrist free from the desk; keep the
  right arm well out from the side; keep the right hand in front of the eyes;
  keep a right angle at the right elbow, and remember that the propelling power
  is located above the right elbow. If you think you are in a good position for
  writing, test the movement without touching the pen to the paper, and study
  the conditions under which you are trying to work. Be sure you are right
  before you go ahead.
]

